# Minimal Bazel configuration for cpp-build-systems-compared.
#
# This project uses the *classic* WORKSPACE model (see WORKSPACE + BUILD.bazel);
# it does NOT provide a MODULE.bazel. Modern Bazel / bazelisk default to Bzlmod,
# which would ignore WORKSPACE and break the build. Force the WORKSPACE path so
# CI matches the locally verified build.
#
# The flag lives under a `ci` config so it is applied ONLY when CI runs
# `bazel ... --config=ci`. This keeps the flag out of the way of older local
# Bazel builds that predate the option, while guaranteeing modern CI Bazel
# (installed via bazelisk, which defaults to Bzlmod) uses the WORKSPACE path.
#
# `--noenable_bzlmod` is the negation of the boolean `--enable_bzlmod` flag and
# is valid for Bazel 6.3 through 8.x (the versions that still support WORKSPACE).
common:ci --noenable_bzlmod
